{
  "summary": "LibreOffice Writer provides multiple view options to display documents according to different needs. The Print Layout option displays the document as it will appear when printed, whereas Web Layout displays it as it would appear in a web browser, making it ideal for creating HTML documents. Users can access Full Screen mode through the View menu to edit documents or present them on a projector, and press the Escape key to exit. To adjust page magnification, the Zoom option in the View menu opens the Zoom and View Layout dialog box. Within this dialog, Zoom Factor includes settings such as Optimal, Fit width and height, Fit to width, 100% view, and a Variable field for custom zoom percentages. Furthermore, the View Layout section allows users to display pages sequentially one below another using Single page, or side by side using the Automatic option. Document view layouts and zoom can also be quickly adjusted using controls on the Writer status bar, including single column and book modes.",
